# 低频词汇 List01
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025恋练有词
# 描述: 低频词汇List01核心词汇

abide /əˈbaɪd/ v. 遵守 You must abide by the rules. 你必须遵守规则。
abolish /əˈbɒlɪʃ/ v. 废除 The parliament voted to abolish the outdated law. 议会投票废除了过时的法律。
abstain /əbˈsteɪn/ v. 弃权；戒绝 Three members abstained from voting. 三名成员弃权。
acclaim /əˈkleɪm/ n./v. 称赞 The film received critical acclaim. 这部电影获得了评论界的好评。
acquaint /əˈkweɪnt/ v. 使熟悉 Please acquaint yourself with the guidelines. 请熟悉一下指南。
adhere /ədˈhɪə(r)/ v. 遵守；粘附 All members must adhere to the code of conduct. 所有成员必须遵守行为准则。
adjacent /əˈdʒeɪsnt/ adj. 邻近的 The park is adjacent to the school. 公园与学校相邻。
advent /ˈædvent/ n. 出现；到来 The advent of the internet changed communication. 互联网的出现改变了沟通方式。
affirm /əˈfɜːm/ v. 肯定 The court affirmed the lower court's decision. 法院肯定了下级法院的裁决。
aggregate /ˈæɡrɪɡeɪt/ v./adj. 聚合；总计 The aggregate score determines the winner. 总分决定获胜者。
alleviate /əˈliːvieɪt/ v. 缓和 The medicine helped alleviate the pain. 药物帮助缓解了疼痛。
alliance /əˈlaɪəns/ n. 联盟 The two countries formed a military alliance. 两国结成了军事联盟。
allot /əˈlɒt/ v. 分配 Each student was allotted 30 minutes for the test. 每个学生被分配了30分钟的考试时间。
amend /əˈmend/ v. 修正 The constitution was amended to expand voting rights. 宪法被修正以扩大选举权。
amid /əˈmɪd/ prep. 在…之中 The company grew amid the economic downturn. 公司在经济低迷中成长了。
analogy /əˈnælədʒi/ n. 类比 The teacher used an analogy to explain the concept. 老师用类比来解释这个概念。
annex /əˈneks/ v./n. 兼并；附属建筑 The country annexed the territory in 1945. 该国在1945年兼并了这块领土。
apparatus /ˌæpəˈreɪtəs/ n. 机构；装置 The state apparatus controls the economy. 国家机构控制着经济。
apprehend /ˌæprɪˈhend/ v. 理解；逮捕 She struggled to apprehend the complexity of the issue. 她难以理解这个问题的复杂性。
array /əˈreɪi/ n. 一系列 The store offers a wide array of products. 商店提供各种各样的产品。
ascertain /ˌæsəˈteɪn/ v. 确定 The police are trying to ascertain the cause of the fire. 警方正在试图确定火灾的原因。
aspiration /ˌæspəˈreɪʃn/ n. 抱负 She has aspirations of becoming a scientist. 她有成为科学家的抱负。
assent /əˈsent/ n./v. 同意 The board gave its assent to the proposal. 董事会对提案表示同意。
attorney /əˈtɜːni/ n. 律师 She hired an attorney to handle the case. 她聘请了一名律师处理此案。
augment /ɔːɡˈment/ v. 增加 They augmented their income with part-time work. 他们通过兼职增加了收入。
avert /əˈvɜːt/ v. 防止 Timely intervention averted a crisis. 及时的干预防止了一场危机。
bail /beɪl/ n./v. 保释 The suspect was released on bail. 嫌疑人被保释。
benign /bɪˈnaɪn/ adj. 良性的；温和的 The tumor was found to be benign. 肿瘤被发现是良性的。
bizarre /bɪˈzɑː(r)/ adj. 奇异的 The plot of the movie is bizarre. 这部电影的情节很奇异。
blaze /bleɪz/ n./v. 火焰；燃烧 A blaze broke out in the warehouse. 仓库里发生了大火。
